<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Br J Cancer</journal-id><journal-title>British Journal of Cancer</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0007-0920</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1532-1827</issn></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">7426318</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2010360</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Nutrition and age at first birth in breast-cancer risk.</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Pawlega</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Wallace</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>6</month><year>1980</year></pub-date><volume>41</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>941</fpage><lpage>945</lpage><abstract><p>Urban/rural breast-cancer incidence ratios in the state of Iowa for 1950 and 1969-71 were contrasted with corresponding urban and rural distributions of age-at-first-birth and population nutrition, variable measured approximately 15 years before each morbidity survey and putatively related to breast-cancer incidence. Over the study interval, the decline in the urban/rural breast-cancer incidence ratio correlated better with changing nutritional patterns than with changing age-at-first-birth.</p></abstract></article-meta></front><body><supplementary-material content-type="scanned-pages"><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00465-0086.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="941" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00465-0087.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="942" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00465-0088.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="943" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00465-0089.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="944" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00465-0090.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="945" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/></supplementary-material></body></article>